        "title": "CLI double space converts to newline",
        "summary": "Added logic in `npm-app/src/cli.ts` to detect double spaces and convert them to newlines. The `keypress` handler now checks if the previous two characters are spaces and inserts a newline if true. This change affects the CLI input handling mechanism.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T17:18:28.059Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When you're typing in the command-line tool and press the space bar twice in a row, the tool now automatically converts that into a paragraph break instead of just adding extra space. This affects anyone typing commands or input directly into the terminal interface. You would notice that typing two spaces no longer creates awkward gaps in your input - it cleanly moves your next text to a new line.",
